# First week on {{project.name}}

Learn what "right" looks like before testing anything. Tick each item when it's done.
You can hand most of these to Claude Code: say _"Do step 3 of docs/qa/FIRST-WEEK.md"_.

- [ ] **1. Read the spec end to end**{{#unless sources.prd}} (ask for it: none is linked yet){{/unless}}, including "out of scope". Note every role, state and rule in `test-plan.md`.
{{#if has_designs}}
- [ ] **2. Map every design screen** (Figma connector){{#if has_web}}: web{{/if}}{{#if has_mobile}}, mobile{{/if}}{{#if has_admin}}, admin{{/if}}{{#if sends_email}}, emails{{/if}}. List frames per screen in `test-plan.md`.
{{else}}
- [ ] **2. Ask for the designs.** If there are none, agree with the team what "right" is (previous build, spec, a style guide).
{{/if}}
- [ ] **3. Fill in the impact grid** (`impact-grid.md`): which roles can be in which states.
- [ ] **4. Check the tools work:**
{{#if portals}}
  - [ ] `npm run smoke` passes for {{#each portals}}{{name}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{#if sends_email}}
  - [ ] the mailbox connector can read {{#if has_mailbox}}{{mailbox.address}}{{else}}the tester inbox (set one up first){{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if has_designs}}
  - [ ] the Figma connector can open the design files
{{/if}}
{{#if mobile.android}}
  - [ ] `adb devices` shows {{#if mobile.real_phone}}the phone{{else}}the emulators{{/if}}; emulators made with `scripts/mobile/emulator-setup.sh create`
{{/if}}
{{#if mobile.ios}}
  - [ ] `scripts/mobile/ios.sh devices` lists the {{mobile.ios_simulator}} simulator, and the developers have given you a simulator build
{{/if}}
{{#if has_saved_sessions}}
  - [ ] one test user per role signed in with `npm run save-session` (email-code or SSO sign-in)
{{/if}}
- [ ] **5. Create test users**: one lane per role ({{#each roles}}{{name}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}), following `agents/fixture-recipe.md`. Fill in "Getting a user into a state".
- [ ] **6. Write the flow backlog** (`flow-backlog.md`): every flow, in the order they matter.
- [ ] **7. Run the first flow end to end** at smoke depth for every role. Save lessons in `LESSONS.md`.
- [ ] **8. Update `handoff.md`.** From now on, keep it current at the end of every session.
